====================================================================
ASSIGNMENT 1
Use the DEPTREE view to generate all the dependencies
for DEPT table.
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

Step 1 : Run the DEPTREE Script
-------------------------------

sql> CONNECT SYS/password AS SYSDBA;

sql> @?/rdbms/admin/utldtree.sql

Output:
-------

Table created.
View created.
Procedure created.

(Note: This script creates the DEPTREE_TEMPTAB table,
DEPTREE view and IDEPTREE view.)


====================================================================
Step 2 : Execute the DEPTREE_FILL Procedure
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> EXEC DEPTREE_FILL('TABLE','SCOTT','DEPT');

Output:
-------

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


====================================================================
Step 3 : Display Dependencies
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> SELECT NESTED_LEVEL,
            TYPE,
            SCHEMA,
            NAME
     FROM DEPTREE
     ORDER BY SEQ#;

Output:
-------

NESTED_LEVEL   TYPE        SCHEMA   NAME
------------   ----------  -------  ----------------
0              TABLE       SCOTT    DEPT
1              VIEW        SCOTT    V3
1              PROCEDURE   SCOTT    ADD_DEPT
1              PROCEDURE   SCOTT    UPDATE_DEPT
1              PROCEDURE   SCOTT    DELETE_DEPT
1              PACKAGE     SCOTT    PK1
1              PACKAGE     SCOTT    PK2
1              PACKAGE     SCOTT    PK3
1              TRIGGER     SCOTT    TRG_V3

9 rows selected.


====================================================================
Alternative Query
====================================================================

sql> SELECT *
     FROM DEPTREE;

Output:
-------

Displays the complete dependency hierarchy of the DEPT table,
including all dependent Views, Procedures, Packages,
Functions and Triggers.


====================================================================
Explanation
====================================================================

The DEPTREE utility is an Oracle supplied utility used to
display object dependencies.

The procedure DEPTREE_FILL populates the DEPTREE view with
dependency information for a specified object.

Syntax:
-------

EXEC DEPTREE_FILL('OBJECT_TYPE','OWNER','OBJECT_NAME');

Example:
--------

EXEC DEPTREE_FILL('TABLE','SCOTT','DEPT');

